    {
      "id": "brief",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Ledger \u2014 design canvas\n\nWarm neutral chrome in both themes, per the brief. The saturation is in the data:\ngreen #00FF00, red #FF0000, gold #FFD400, cyan #00E5FF, violet #A020FF on dark \u2014\nthe same hues dropped in lightness on light. No glow: the colours carry themselves.\n\nReal figures throughout, taken from data.json at 2 Sep 2026.\nStatic mockups, not a clickable prototype."
    },
    {
      "id": "themes",
      "x": 1560,
      "y": -200,
      "w": 640,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "Both themes shown on real screens: Portfolio, Gold and Stocks in dark;\nReal Estate and the states board in light."
    },
    {
      "id": "newscope",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 900,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "A BETTER STRUCTURE \u2014 read \"The model\" first\n\nCash accounts, gold, a car, a property and a brokerage book are all the same thing:\nsomewhere value sits. One typed list of nodes \u2014 cash, asset, liability, external \u2014\nand every event becomes a transaction whose legs move value between them.\n\nThat covers an exchange, an expense, a gold purchase, a stock funding and an\ninstallment payment with one mechanism instead of four, and net worth becomes\none rule: assets minus liabilities.\n\nIt is a bigger rebuild than a port, and rule zero still binds \u2014 every F-### must\nstill produce the same number. ARCHITECTURE.md \u00a710 has the schema and the cost."
    }
  ],
